  "notes": [
   "Inputs are recipe ingredients and recognized machine fuels or fluids supplied from outside. Outputs are products not consumed by another included process. Check belt, pipe, and robot connections in-game; this analysis does not simulate routing or throughput.",
   "Supply every labeled operating input, including fluids where listed, and external electricity. Preserve stock controls, circuit wires and passive-provider chest limits. Intermediates are manufactured inside; construction materials are not operating inputs.",
   "Factorio 2.1.24 Space Age, normal quality: AM2 and chemical plants, no modules, red belts, fast and bulk inserters, substations. WEST entrances north to south: sulfuric acid (pipe), plastic, copper, iron, steel (belts), lubricant (pipe). EAST: one passive provider chest with independent caps 50 construction robots, 50 logistic robots, 10 roboports, 50 storage chests, 50 passive provider chests. All circuits, cable, gears, pipes, engines, batteries, frames and steel chests are made inside. Preserve the red ring wires (per-tile hold readers), the green chest and token wires, filters and caps. Supply electricity at any substation; the three are wired together.",
   "Leave the shared chest unrestricted (no bar). Caps: 50 construction robots, 50 logistic robots, 10 roboports, 50 storage chests, 50 passive provider chests; they live in the five filter deciders. The chest has 48 slots and the five products at their caps fill five.",
   "The entrance panels show recipe totals at the targets. The production tokens run the products a little above target, so plan supply for the measured draw in the README, not for the panels.",
   "Do not remove the red wires from ring tiles or the circuit conditions on the arms; the three arms on the west edge (plastic, iron, steel) are the ring entrances.",
   "Game profile: Factorio 2.1.25."
  ]
 },
